<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch March producer prices rise 2.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch March producer prices rise 2.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch producer price index (PPI) for manufactured goods rose a provisional 0.2 percent in March from February, giving a 2.2 percent rise year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p> DUTCH PRODUCER PRICES	  March 97    Feb 97    March 96</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		103.5	103.3	101.3</p>
<p> Month-on-month pct change     +0.2	 -0.2	 +0.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year pct change	 +2.2	 +2.5	 +0.5</p>
<p> Subindex domestic prices     106.9	106.8	105.4</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		  +1.4	 +1.6	 +1.2</p>
<p> Subindex export prices	 100.8	100.6	 98.2</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		  +2.6	 +3.2	 +0.1</p>
<p>The CBS said lower oil prices had pressured March PPI somewhat compared to January and February 1997.</p>
<p>Prices in the food industry were 2.8 percent higher in March compared to a year earlier, partly due to rising pork prices.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
